  "versionLocalizations": {
    "1.1.3": [
      {
        "id": "86ae2909-67b5-4f6e-8bfa-773b6c41e17f",
        "description": "Log real sets, reps and weight. Every set earns XP.\nRank up through 24 ranks and fight 24 bosses with your team.\nFree to play. No ads.\n\nA REAL WORKOUT LOG\n• Strength, cardio, timed holds, heavy bag rounds, classes and sports\n• See what you lifted last time and repeat it in one tap\n• Repeat your last workout, or start from a saved routine\n• Runs and rides keep distance, time and pace\n• Personal records found for you, with bonuses for beating your last session\n\nA GAME THAT REWARDS SHOWING UP\n• Every workout pays XP and coins\n• 24 ranks, from Recruit to Legend\n• Gear drops that make your warrior stronger\n• Weekly goals and streak bonuses for training on schedule\n\nTRAIN WITH A TEAM\n• Make or join a team and pick one of 18 themes\n• Your workouts power team battles against 24 bosses, from goblins to titans\n• A team feed with reactions, and a team rank you climb together\n\nSEE YOUR FUTURE SELF\n• Add a photo and get an AI image of the body your plan is building\n\nFAIR PLAY\n• Clear scoring rules and honest weight limits, so every rank is earned\n\nDeparture is free to download and play. Optional purchases include coin packs, XP boosts, equipment slots and banners.",
        "locale": "en-US",
        "keywords": "workout,tracker,lifting,weightlifting,strength,exercise,game,gamified,rpg,xp,habit,team,monster,raid",
        "marketingUrl": "https://departure.engagequalia.com",
        "promotionalText": "New: repeat your last workout in three taps and keep every set in your routines. Your lifts earn XP. Your team fights bosses. Free, no ads.",
        "supportUrl": "https://departure.engagequalia.com/support",
        "whatsNew": "Departure has a new look. The purple is gone, and the app now uses cold slate and ice blue with bolder headings. The Arena is simpler. You can be on one team at a time, and the four modes sit in two rows: training and Skirmish against people on top, and Monster Ambush and Warpath against monsters below, from easier to harder. Monster Ambush fights now play out on screen, with your warrior and the monster clashing in every round. Skirmish shows only real teams, with a clear scoreboard and a picture of the two teams meeting. Making a battle scene after a Skirmish works again. Training Grounds now suggests one workout each day, picked from the area you have trained least. New players get a short full body workout with no weights. The Campfire is cleaner, with Overview, Roster and Chat at the top. Home and Train show more at a glance: today's challenge, your goal days, your streak and the XP you earned this week. The exercise picker lists the exercises you have done before first, with what you did last time. On the Equip board, boots now sit in their own tall frame."
      }
    ]
